      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Maple Leafs woke up on the eve of the season with the sort of thump that changes a room - a blockbuster, a contract, and a new face expected to ride shotgun with Auston Matthews. <strong>Toronto landed Kirill Marchenko in the Matthew Knies deal and locked him up for six years at $75 million</strong>, a hard-handed bet from John Chayka that says the club wants more speed, more finish, and fewer long debates about the top six. The numbers still read 0-0-0, first in the Atlantic, but that's preseason bookkeeping now; the real ledger opens tonight against Montreal. Knies is gone, Marchenko is here, and the lineup projections already look different. <strong>What matters next is whether Marchenko can settle in fast and turn all this noise into a clean opening-night start</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated September 29, 2026"
      },
