      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The curtain has dropped, and now the Blue Jays must sort through the wreckage with a clear eye - not nostalgia. <strong>Shane Bieber and Myles Straw both hope to return as Toronto's market opens</strong>, and that is the first real offseason test for a club that finished 79-83 and fifth in the AL East. Bieber gives them rotation credibility; Straw, at least, gives them a glove worth debating against an $8 million decision that suddenly looks sharp-edged. The bigger issue is direction. A team built to contend never found enough punch, and the front office has to decide whether to keep patching or start reshaping. <strong>What matters now is whether Toronto turns that free-agent uncertainty into a cleaner roster before winter hardens the market</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated September 29, 2026"
