        "body": "Training camp has a pulse again in Toronto - and it's beating to Kawhi Leonard's old, familiar drum. <strong>Leonard's return to the Raptors</strong> gives this group a bona fide headliner, the sort of presence that changes every drill, every rotation chart, every conversation in the gym. The club arrives in Quebec City with a fresh start and a first preseason test against Miami on Saturday at 7 p.m. ET, before the real measuring stick lands Oct. 21 against Chicago. The Raptors are asking a lot of a roster built on length, youth and timing, and Leonard's health will steer everything; Darko Rajakovic knows it, the room knows it, and so does anyone who's watched this league long enough. <strong>What matters now is how quickly Leonard meshes with Scottie Barnes and the rest of the new-look group before the preseason opens.</strong>",
