        "body": "The Commanders finally have a little wind at their backs - but it came with a price, as <strong>the 33-31 stunner over Seattle</strong> lifted them to 1-2 and third in the NFC East, one game back, while the defense spent the next morning counting bodies. Leo Chenal's season-ending neck surgery is the sort of blow that hangs over a locker room, and Jayden Daniels' return trip to London is the story that gives Washington oxygen. The kid is expected to travel and practice, which matters because Marcus Mariota steadied the ship, but this offense still belongs to Daniels when he's right. Austin Ekeler's arrival adds a veteran edge, another crease-finder for a team that needs every inch. <strong>Next comes Sunday in London against the Colts - and it will tell us whether this win was a rescue or a turning point.</strong>",
