      "title": "Leafs Open With Canadiens Visit",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Maple Leafs open their season tonight against the Canadiens at 7 p.m. ET at Scotiabank Arena, with Sportsnet carrying the game and Bobrovsky likely starting in goal against Dobes. Toronto also lists Marchenko as day to day, though not for injury-related reasons.",
        "It is a busy Toronto sports morning. The Blue Jays are in their offseason, with offseason chatter centering on Bieber and Straw as they hope for a return to the club. The Raptors are at training camp and will play their next preseason game against the Heat on Saturday at 7 p.m. ET, while their regular season starts Oct. 21 at home against the Bulls. For the Commanders, Jayden Daniels is expected to travel with the team to London and practice this week ahead of the Oct. 4 game against the Colts on NFL Net."
